## Validation finding that must carry forward

Two five-fold protocols are frozen:

- `fold_state_stratified` — primary.
- `fold_municipality_grouped` — spatial/generalization robustness.

The municipality-grouped protocol is much harder. Representative baseline RMSE:

```text
state-stratified ExtraTrees A7   0.4966
municipality-grouped Ridge A3    0.7426
municipality-grouped ExtraTrees A6 0.8835
```

Do not optimize only the easier state-stratified metric. Spatial/municipal generalization is a
first-class risk.

## Historical clean/competition distinction

The repository still preserves both feature labels for provenance, but **active modeling from
03C.2 onward uses only `competition`**.

`clean`
: historical/static provenance label only; do not benchmark or select models on this track unless explicitly reopened.

`competition`
: active modeling track = clean plus rule-permitted 2025/full-season/contemporaneous public covariates.

The exact operational forecast cutoff is still unresolved. Do not describe competition-mode
features as a strict prospective forecast.

SIAP 2025 is a competition-only municipal outcome proxy and must stay explicitly labeled.

## Feature QC finding

Only one CHIRPS daily competition feature survives in Feature Table v1. Most candidate CHIRPS
daily aggregates were dropped as all-null by the builder. Investigate before claiming a rich
CHIRPS contribution.

Train-versus-prediction screening flagged only 6/1401 numeric features under the configured
descriptive shift/support thresholds. These X-only diagnostics are not labels and must not be
used as a hidden-test tuning target.

## Modeling-track directive — competition only

From Checkpoint 03C.2 onward, **use only the `competition` feature track** for model
development, tuning, comparison and final prediction.

Operational meaning:

```text
competition = clean + competition-mode features
clean       = historical/diagnostic only; do not run unless explicitly reopened
```

Do not spend compute comparing clean versus competition and do not use clean results to select
the 03C.2 model. The project objective is the FIRA competition estimate after observing the
2025 cycle, so current modeling prioritizes the competition representation.

CHIRPS remains excluded pending QC even though the active track is competition.

## Checkpoint 03C.1 representation benchmark

Implementation is on the current 03C branch and should be run with:

```text
python tools/run_checkpoint_03c.py
```

It evaluates both `clean` and `competition` tracks with:

```text
B0 base
B1 agronomic only
B2 empirical only
B3 base + agronomic
B4 base + empirical
B5 base + agronomic + empirical
B7 B5 + fold-local discovered expressions
```

using fixed Ridge10 and ExtraTrees under both frozen Checkpoint 02 protocols. CHIRPS is
excluded pending QC. The run reports pooled OOF metrics as well as mean-fold metrics and
does not score the 59 hidden-target parcels. Broad tuning/CatBoost/kernels/PCA/PLS belong to
03C.2 after these representation results are reviewed.

## 03C.2 checkpoint snapshot

The workstation benchmark is complete and committed.

```text
active track: competition only
representations: C0, C1, C2, C3
outer CV: frozen state-stratified + municipality-grouped
inner CV: 3-fold, aligned to outer protocol
models: Ridge, ElasticNet, ExtraTrees, CatBoost, PLS, PCA+RBF KRR, PCA+Poly2 KRR
individual finalists frozen: C0+PLS, C3+Ridge, C1+CatBoost
CatBoost execution: GPU
59 predictions generated: no
```

Key 03C.2 municipality-grouped OOF RMSE: C0+PLS 0.7621, C3+Ridge 0.7650, C1+CatBoost 0.7709. ExtraTrees remains stronger under state-stratified CV but is less robust under municipality-grouped CV.

## Modeling rules for Checkpoint 03

Reuse `reports/checkpoint_02/cv_folds.csv`.

Candidate families may include CatBoost, Ridge/ElasticNet, ExtraTrees/RandomForest,
HistGradientBoosting and LightGBM/XGBoost if justified.

Because n=138 and p is large, keep searches disciplined.

Any learned preprocessing must be inside folds:

- imputation;
- scaling;
- PCA/PLS;
- supervised feature selection;
- encoding;
- target-aware transforms.

Keep fold-level RMSE/MAE/R² and machine-readable experiment records.

Do not regenerate folds because a result is inconvenient.

## Repository rules

Source evidence:

```text
data/source/
docs/official/
docs/reference/
```

must not be edited to fit code.

Stable reusable logic belongs under `src/geocebada/`.

Notebooks orchestrate exploration; they are not the canonical implementation.

Before adding a public helper, inspect `docs/FUNCTION_INDEX.md`.

For Streamlit/deployment work, read `app/AGENTS.md` first.

Large external raw/interim data remain gitignored. The deliberate processed-data exceptions are canonical `data/processed/features_v1/`, `data/processed/agronomic_features_v1/` and `data/processed/empirical_features_v1/`, all versioned.

Material AI-assisted work must be recorded in `docs/AI_USAGE.md`.

